were analyzed using stepped collision energy (SCE) HCD-MS2-MS3 acquisition strategy. (SCE) HCD MS2 was triggered for charge states +4 to +8 and CID-MS3 was triggered if a unique mass difference (Δ=31.9721) was observed in the MS2 spectrum for two of the signature peaks. Orbitrap mass resolution was set to 120,000 (MS1) and 60,000 (MS2). MS3 scans were acquired in the ion trap. Isolation windows were set to 1.6 m/z at MS1 level and 2.5 m/z at MS2 level. The collision energy was 21-27-33% for (SCE) HCD-MS2 and 35% for CID-MS3. Top speed of 5 sec for non FAIMS or single CV experiments and 2 sec/CV for internal stepping was used. Dynamic exclusion was set to 30, 45 or 60 sec. for increasing LC-gradient. Protein identification and abundance estimation were performed using an LTQ Orbitrap Elite mass spectrometer (Thermo Fisher Scientific) and 180 min linear gradients.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
